#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "434e9983-5bd2-56c7-a949-f56896edd2ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d93faf01-991d-51e3-8236-844afb9915c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377398} {:answer/id #uuid "31cebca5-0c8e-5cea-924a-e88cdac49051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377399} {:answer/id #uuid "5abb14df-61c6-5287-9d4d-4c5c8ffda741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377400} {:answer/id #uuid "4e460218-3cc5-5f89-acfd-95fb5dae3c56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377401} {:answer/id #uuid "83fe33a9-cdcf-508a-b12c-851fd20be89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31cebca5-0c8e-5cea-924a-e88cdac49051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377399} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b408c9-e40b-5275-834e-9e3147937942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0009bcce-6e01-5a84-a1f7-a258d2553d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161488" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{x+y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{10}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b901242c-eea0-5b94-9082-042ff7341911" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type I Region Using a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e56d5d-939a-5351-8fe4-a2542fae9dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377405} {:answer/id #uuid "e29e605b-eb4b-57fe-949a-99a838e72058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377406} {:answer/id #uuid "b86f6365-6af8-5fe9-ba9d-b0fe18ca9237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377407} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7c6f93-c9d5-5eeb-8a20-f7643e28c8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377408} {:answer/id #uuid "e0abc0ea-15ae-5030-8512-fad06da9d2ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e56d5d-939a-5351-8fe4-a2542fae9dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377405} :answer-field/id #uuid "d22d7a49-a0a3-5e36-87ee-64c4d247f33e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6452405b-e1dd-5ae2-81b6-5cbbf8a1c501" :question/math-academy-id "q-161514" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/330b550b31987e29aceb4b2a253e26ebec470692a6a0144f64725801f2df2b7d.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above. \n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/03a91dfd9f6a69455157c47162b11cd69cb3b03cfabea2770b94f7322015b0e2.png)\n\n \nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/ac3eafe926b84588703bb8a56a1529ebe1352d25764a523b97c684a4f4e95201.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[xz]_{z=0}^{z=1+2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx & =[3{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b901242c-eea0-5b94-9082-042ff7341911" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type I Region Using a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34bbc517-4971-52c5-ae8a-31fec81e5152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377412} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf7e1ba-b4ed-511d-826f-a4c3ecd9482b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377413} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0a361b-bbb9-5110-8d6c-f9cd6e5ae74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377414} {:answer/id #uuid "82f3920b-3ed9-5e3b-ab66-08fd9c0f65a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377415} {:answer/id #uuid "95e3a82e-676f-5085-8d1f-ada44e3173b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc0a361b-bbb9-5110-8d6c-f9cd6e5ae74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377414} :answer-field/id #uuid "1632c9f4-64ef-5690-b803-e2fd26ea3fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4d3d9e94-e68a-5c9a-8df0-3e8abb69376b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161517" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/89fba52c9a48d4f8f2ddac0b060c3ffab7e3ba4f6652124f4a9ac6ba39a579e5.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/86c1bef04ebf536b10f3f7d61eafcff909bd439b7641cbfc31cecd05cca23c18.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/dfa0a80bc323401f050d1302dc42c92558d8b566d9b0f985e955d34eb5cc15bd.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)[z]_{z=0}^{z=2-x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)(2-x+y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)y+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{3x-1}{2}\\,{y}^{2}+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)y]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2(3x-1)+2(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx & =[-2{x}^{3}+10x-6x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(-2+10-6)-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "434e9983-5bd2-56c7-a949-f56896edd2ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d39b59a8-c947-589a-9d67-ebfe07a4311b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197510} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c82be4-29db-586a-9cd0-ef3eda5e20fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197511} {:answer/id #uuid "fd618ee4-d7ff-5bb5-8ae1-eb1721b5b21f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197512} {:answer/id #uuid "47ca7f1b-3942-5bd3-8f9d-ab570252e09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197513} {:answer/id #uuid "58b92553-5c56-5c09-992a-7af7a554032f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d39b59a8-c947-589a-9d67-ebfe07a4311b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197510} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6d0698e-cb4a-56cf-8372-e60701e081db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5921e826-710a-5d93-8c85-d28de47fab13" :question/math-academy-id "q-38532" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2((x+y)^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{x}^{2}y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x-0)+2x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6361ca8e-40c3-558b-aae5-1b2a68d02633" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86f66acc-bc79-5bdd-9149-cc2c05e028a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197528} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8de676-c420-578d-b1cf-82eb10cb4720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197529} {:answer/id #uuid "c239a86a-3bf9-50c4-abb4-cc93be51a498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197530} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf3bdf3-d123-5251-ad4c-06f18d91d69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197531} {:answer/id #uuid "724bc1bb-937c-5ec6-98d3-455a812db1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bf3bdf3-d123-5251-ad4c-06f18d91d69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197531} :answer-field/id #uuid "50a79c5e-641c-5efb-bd03-fdbd9dfb2ff6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cabc579-f309-591e-be01-d99bc3ea5808" :question/math-academy-id "q-38783" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type I region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x-y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[30xz]_{z=0}^{z=1-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x(1-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[30xy-30{x}^{2}y-15x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}30x(1-x)-30{x}^{2}(1-x)-15x(1-x)^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx & ={[\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{4}-10{x}^{3}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4}-10+\\frac{15}{2})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
